Project Demonstration Phase

The Project Demonstration Phase is the stage where the completed project is presented and explained to the users, teachers, or evaluators.

Main Points:

Introduce the Project – Explain the project title, purpose, and objectives.
Explain Features – Describe the main functions and benefits of the project.
Show Working Demo – Demonstrate how the project works step by step.
Answer Questions – Respond to questions and doubts from evaluators.
Collect Feedback – Get suggestions and feedback for future improvements.
